# Module Structure

Follow the canonical folder structure defined in `docs/module-structure.md` for every feature module.

## Canonical Layout

```
src/{module-name}/
├── {module-name}.module.ts
├── __fixtures__/
│   └── {module-name}.fixtures.ts
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/
│   ├── events/
│   ├── errors/
│   └── ports/
├── application/
│   ├── use-cases/
│   ├── handlers/
│   └── dto/
├── infrastructure/
│   ├── repositories/
│   └── services/
└── presentation/
    ├── {module-name}.controller.ts
    └── dto/
```

## File Naming

- Entities: `{name}.entity.ts`
- Value objects: `{name}.value-object.ts`
- Events: `{entity}.events.ts`
- Errors: `{module}.error-codes.ts`, `{module}.errors.ts`, `{module}.error-factory.ts`
- Ports: `{entity}.repository.port.ts`
- Use cases: `{action}.use-case.ts`
- Handlers: `{entity}-activity.handler.ts`
- DTOs (application): `{action}.input.ts`, `{entity}.output.ts`
- Repositories: `{entity}.repository.ts`
- Services: `{service-name}.service.ts`
- Controllers: `{module-name}.controller.ts`
- DTOs (presentation): `{action}.input.dto.ts`, `{entity}.output.dto.ts`
- Tests: co-located as `{name}.spec.ts`

## Scaffolding Order (Inside-Out)

1. Domain entities and value objects
2. Domain events with schemas
3. Domain errors and error factory
4. Domain port interfaces with DI tokens
5. Application DTOs
6. Application use cases
7. Application event handlers
8. Infrastructure repositories
9. Infrastructure services
10. Presentation DTOs
11. Presentation controllers
12. Module file with DI wiring
13. Register in `app.module.ts`

## Reference

See `docs/module-structure.md` for detailed layer responsibilities, dependency direction, and reference module examples.
